{
 "uid": "env-promotion",
 "title": "Promotion Pipeline \u2014 dev, staging, prod",
 "schemaVersion": 39,
 "tags": [
  "delivery",
  "promotion",
  "rollout"
 ],
 "time": {
  "from": "now-1h",
  "to": "now"
 },
 "refresh": "30s",
 "editable": true,
 "graphTooltip": 1,
 "annotations": {
  "list": []
 },
 "templating": {
  "list": []
 },
 "panels": [
  {
   "title": "Where the release actually is",
   "type": "text",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 5,
    "w": 24,
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "A promotion is an image moving forward one environment at a time. The table below is the pipeline's live state: each namespace and the tag its pods were **asked** to run.\n\nRead `image_spec`, not `image`. The lab builds every version as both `vX.Y.Z` and `:latest`, so those tags share a digest and the kubelet reports whichever one it resolved \u2014 usually `docker.io/library/{{.WorkloadName}}:latest` for a pod that correctly requested `{{.WorkloadName}}:v1.1.0`. `image_spec` is what the pod asked for, and that is the release.\n\nThe right-hand panel is the difference between asking and arriving: **rollout converged** sits at 1 while an environment is settled, dips during a promotion, and *stays down* when a promotion cannot land \u2014 a tag that was never built, for instance. That is drift, and it is what `verify` fails on."
   }
  },
  {
   "title": "The pipeline right now \u2014 which tag each environment asked for",
   "type": "table",
   "description": "One row per environment. During a promotion two rows appear for the same namespace: the old ReplicaSet's pod and the new one.",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 8,
    "w": 13,
    "x": 0,
    "y": 5
   },
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "custom": {
      "align": "left"
     }
    },
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "showHeader": true
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "kube_pod_container_info{namespace=~\"env-.*\"}",
     "instant": true,
     "format": "table",
     "refId": "A"
    }
   ],
   "transformations": [
    {
     "id": "organize",
     "options": {
      "excludeByName": {
       "Time": true,
       "Value": true,
       "__name__": true,
       "container": true,
       "endpoint": true,
       "instance": true,
       "job": true,
       "pod": true,
       "service": true,
       "uid": true,
       "image_id": true,
       "container_id": true,
       "image": true
      },
      "renameByName": {
       "namespace": "environment",
       "image_spec": "requested image"
      }
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Rollout converged (1 = settled, below 1 = drifting)",
   "type": "timeseries",
   "description": "A rollout has converged when every desired replica runs the new template and is available. Updated replicas alone count a new pod that is stuck in ImagePullBackOff, so a release that can never land would read as settled; subtracting the unavailable ones is what makes it show as drifting.",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 8,
    "w": 11,
    "x": 13,
    "y": 5
   },
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "unit": "none",
     "min": 0,
     "custom": {
      "drawStyle": "line",
      "lineWidth": 2,
      "fillOpacity": 10,
      "spanNulls": false,
      "stacking": {
       "mode": "none"
      }
     },
     "max": 1.1
    },
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "legend": {
     "displayMode": "list",
     "placement": "bottom",
     "showLegend": true
    },
    "tooltip": {
     "mode": "multi",
     "sort": "none"
    }
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "(sum by (namespace) (kube_deployment_status_replicas_updated{namespace=~\"env-.*\"}) - sum by (namespace) (kube_deployment_status_replicas_unavailable{namespace=~\"env-.*\"})) / sum by (namespace) (kube_deployment_spec_replicas{namespace=~\"env-.*\"})",
     "legendFormat": "{{namespace}}: updated and available / desired replicas",
     "refId": "A"
    },
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "sum by (namespace) (kube_deployment_status_observed_generation{namespace=~\"env-.*\"}) / sum by (namespace) (kube_deployment_metadata_generation{namespace=~\"env-.*\"})",
     "legendFormat": "{{namespace}}: observed / desired generation",
     "refId": "B"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Ready replicas per environment",
   "type": "timeseries",
   "description": "The dip during a promotion is the new ReplicaSet coming up. A dip that does not recover is a release that never made it \u2014 check the pods for ImagePullBackOff before you blame the app.",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 8,
    "w": 12,
    "x": 0,
    "y": 13
   },
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "unit": "none",
     "min": 0,
     "custom": {
      "drawStyle": "line",
      "lineWidth": 2,
      "fillOpacity": 10,
      "spanNulls": false,
      "stacking": {
       "mode": "none"
      }
     }
    },
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "legend": {
     "displayMode": "list",
     "placement": "bottom",
     "showLegend": true
    },
    "tooltip": {
     "mode": "multi",
     "sort": "none"
    }
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "sum by (namespace) (kube_deployment_status_replicas_available{namespace=~\"env-.*\"})",
     "legendFormat": "{{namespace}}: available",
     "refId": "A"
    },
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "sum by (namespace) (kube_deployment_spec_replicas{namespace=~\"env-.*\"})",
     "legendFormat": "{{namespace}}: desired",
     "refId": "B"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "ReplicaSets per environment \u2014 the release history, live",
   "type": "timeseries",
   "description": "Each new tag an environment is promoted to leaves a ReplicaSet behind; this is 'kubectl rollout history' as a graph. A rollback does NOT add one \u2014 it reuses an older ReplicaSet, which is exactly why rolling back is fast and rebuilding is not.",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 8,
    "w": 12,
    "x": 12,
    "y": 13
   },
   "datasource": {
    "type": "prometheus",
    "uid": "prometheus"
   },
   "fieldConfig": {
    "defaults": {
     "unit": "none",
     "min": 0,
     "custom": {
      "drawStyle": "line",
      "lineWidth": 2,
      "fillOpacity": 10,
      "spanNulls": false,
      "stacking": {
       "mode": "none"
      }
     }
    },
    "overrides": []
   },
   "options": {
    "legend": {
     "displayMode": "list",
     "placement": "bottom",
     "showLegend": true
    },
    "tooltip": {
     "mode": "multi",
     "sort": "none"
    }
   },
   "targets": [
    {
     "datasource": {
      "type": "prometheus",
      "uid": "prometheus"
     },
     "expr": "count by (namespace) (kube_replicaset_owner{namespace=~\"env-.*\"})",
     "legendFormat": "{{namespace}}",
     "refId": "A"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
